      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T20:11:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function has been somewhat cargo-culted from `SkWebpCodec` - see: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/codec/SkWebpCodec.cpp;l\u003d337-366;drc\u003dc9943f14039faa721b02c64b5fad42dfb87af013\n\nThe main difference is that in `SkPngRustCodec` we can guarantee that source and destination use the same `SkColorType` and `SkAlphaType` - we don\u0027t need to account for this like `SkWebpCodec` does.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 263,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 263,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "f523531e90a0f40740763e76314917ab53a84ed5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74f7b104_05657908",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_png/impl/SkPngRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 504,
      "author": {
        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-23T20:11:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This has been just moved from `incrementalDecode` in an attempt to improve readability (by removing interlacing details from `incrementalDecode`).  In theory this has a negative performance impact (the 2 vectors need to be reinitialized), but interlaced images are rare (1-2% of all images in top 500 websites AFAICT), so I think readability should win here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 504,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 504,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "f523531e90a0f40740763e76314917ab53a84ed5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
